 the certificate. The ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"private key stays where its custodian put","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it","type":"text"}]},{"text":" (Vault, or sealed into the row) and is never written to the server volume. A trust","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anchor is public by construction: it is what the server hands every client during the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"TLS handshake, and every device that has to validate the chain already holds a copy. #"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Why a restart rustls builds its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootCertStore"},{"type":"text","text":" once, when the listener is constructed,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and actix-web binds that config for the process’s life. Toggling this changes what the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"next","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" boot trusts, and the API says so in its response rather than pretending the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"change took effect. Defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":", so a deployment that never touches this keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly the TLS posture it has today."}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/GeneratedCaCertificate/fingerprint":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"fingerprint","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fingerprint","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/GeneratedCaCertificate\/fingerprint","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/generatedcacertificate\/fingerprint","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"SHA-256 fingerprint of the certificate.","type":"text"}]